OL,3,GNEWSADeadly horse disease outbreak
OL,4,Aconfirmed in Galloway
OL,5,
OL,6,FVets in south-west Scotland have warned
OL,7,Fhorse owners to be vigilant for a
OL,8,Fdeadly disease after multiple cases and
OL,9,Fdeaths have been recorded across the
OL,10,FWigtownshire area.
OL,12,FMachars Veterinary Services, based in
OL,13,FNewton Stewart, confirmed that it had
OL,14,Fresponded to a spate of Equine Grass
OL,15,FSickness (EGS) cases which had resulted
OL,16,Fin fatalities.
OL,18,FThe disease causes paralysis of the
OL,19,Fdigestive system and, with no vaccine
OL,20,Fand only a few treatments available,
OL,21,Fabout 80% of horses affected will die.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,430,420,260,160,0,100
